                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "I voted NO on the continuing resolution because it will hike health insurance premiums by more than $3,200 annually for 28,000 people in our district who are struggling to pay their bills\u2013and for 20 million other Americans. We also can\u2019t make deals with a White House that won\u2019t comply with the law that we pass (e.g. after DOGE cuts and pocket recissions), so the deal must include protections like the POCCA Act.\n\nThank you to\u00a0@mtnviewellen, the Community Services Agency, @UWBayArea, @TheatreWorksSV,\u00a0SCC Public Health, the Santa Clara County Medical Association,\u00a0@ThriveAlliance and the Silicon Valley Council of Nonprofits for joining me for a press conference to discuss our fight for working people in our community and throughout our nation.",
