                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 2,
                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "The government may reopen soon, but tens of millions of Americans still face sharply higher health insurance premiums next month. That\u2019s why today I introduced the Fix It Act \u2014 a practical, bipartisan approach to cut excessive Medicare Advantage payouts to insurers and use those savings to reduce premiums for millions of Americans so they can afford their health insurance. Let\u2019s fix this, together.",
